WEBVTT

1
00:00:26,794 --> 00:00:31,498
[suspenseful music]

2
00:01:03,497 --> 00:01:06,400
[footsteps]

3
00:01:42,570 --> 00:01:47,407
[wind blowing]

4
00:01:53,081 --> 00:01:56,249
[relaxing music]

5
00:01:56,350 --> 00:01:57,585
[door slamming]

6
00:02:27,280 --> 00:02:28,415
You're Hunter.

7
00:02:33,755 --> 00:02:34,656
I'm Elle.

8
00:02:36,156 --> 00:02:37,525
[Hunter] I know.

9
00:02:38,325 --> 00:02:41,763
I love you...in everything.

10
00:02:48,069 --> 00:02:50,470
You don't have to
sell yourself to me.

11
00:02:50,571 --> 00:02:52,305
[sigh]

12
00:02:54,307 --> 00:02:55,877
I gave away my room.

13
00:02:57,444 --> 00:02:59,446
That's unfortunate.

14
00:02:59,947 --> 00:03:04,152
The airline lost my luggage
because of the mist.

15
00:03:05,218 --> 00:03:06,654
It's been a disaster.

16
00:03:08,089 --> 00:03:10,390
Aren't you the poor
little match girl.

17
00:03:14,162 --> 00:03:16,363
Hans Christian Andersen.

18
00:03:18,132 --> 00:03:20,635
I don't really
listen to European music.

19
00:03:25,973 --> 00:03:26,841
Come on.

20
00:03:33,715 --> 00:03:36,551
I'm just so excited
to be in the movie with you.

21
00:03:36,651 --> 00:03:39,520
[soft romantic orchestral music]

22
00:03:50,064 --> 00:03:53,233
[music continues]

23
00:04:09,884 --> 00:04:12,653
Fuck me.

24
00:04:20,360 --> 00:04:21,829
My room is this way.

25
00:05:25,760 --> 00:05:26,661
Hey.

26
00:05:28,529 --> 00:05:32,934
You know, I can stay on
the couch. It looks super comfy.

27
00:05:34,602 --> 00:05:37,605
You can stay with me.
I'm just taking my face off.

28
00:05:38,940 --> 00:05:41,642
Ok. Cool.

29
00:05:51,484 --> 00:05:53,955
[music ends]

30
00:05:55,156 --> 00:05:57,058
I don't know if
I can post these.

31
00:05:58,326 --> 00:06:01,796
People will say I've
become...unrelatable.

32
00:06:12,740 --> 00:06:15,810
[romantic string orchestra]

33
00:07:16,904 --> 00:07:19,073
[music fades]

34
00:07:26,914 --> 00:07:29,150
[bangle rattling]

35
00:07:29,250 --> 00:07:30,450
Can you help me with this?

36
00:07:36,390 --> 00:07:37,792
[exhaling]

37
00:07:39,527 --> 00:07:41,629
You've got expensive taste.

38
00:07:43,564 --> 00:07:44,799
Play date?

39
00:07:46,834 --> 00:07:49,537
[Dominique] That bangle
hasn't been cool in ages.

40
00:07:49,637 --> 00:07:51,471
It's for the masses.

41
00:07:51,906 --> 00:07:55,609
For the masses? Oh,
you're so unrelatable.

42
00:07:55,710 --> 00:07:56,677
[Dominique] Ew.

43
00:07:56,777 --> 00:07:58,713
Who would want to be relatable?

44
00:08:00,815 --> 00:08:02,550
Hunter wants to be relatable.

45
00:08:03,317 --> 00:08:04,552
It's...

46
00:08:04,652 --> 00:08:05,853
a metrics thing.

47
00:08:05,953 --> 00:08:08,255
Oh...no, no, no.

48
00:08:09,357 --> 00:08:11,125
You can let
the numbers measure you,

49
00:08:11,225 --> 00:08:13,961
but you can't measure yourself
by the numbers.

50
00:08:14,228 --> 00:08:17,698
That's wise. Did you pick
that up at a sound bath?

51
00:08:21,369 --> 00:08:23,170
There's not a single person...

52
00:08:23,270 --> 00:08:24,905
on this planet...

53
00:08:25,006 --> 00:08:26,240
that is like you.

54
00:08:32,546 --> 00:08:33,914
You're a very specific...

55
00:08:34,015 --> 00:08:36,017
spec of stardust.

56
00:08:36,117 --> 00:08:37,218
Stop!

57
00:08:38,486 --> 00:08:40,988
No. You stop!
This means something.

58
00:08:45,226 --> 00:08:46,594
[Dominique] Say it with me.

59
00:08:48,696 --> 00:08:55,569
I am a wholly
unique consciousness.

60
00:08:56,670 --> 00:09:00,441
I am a wholly...

61
00:09:00,541 --> 00:09:04,211
unique consciousness.

62
00:09:05,146 --> 00:09:06,680
And I am made...

63
00:09:07,648 --> 00:09:09,717
of stardust.

64
00:09:10,818 --> 00:09:17,825
I am made of stardust.

65
00:09:19,460 --> 00:09:23,998
The moment you forget that
is the moment you disappear.

66
00:09:33,774 --> 00:09:37,678
I'm sorry, but...who are you?

67
00:09:39,346 --> 00:09:41,215
I'd like you to meet Dominique.

68
00:09:46,687 --> 00:09:48,523
My step mom.

69
00:09:48,622 --> 00:09:53,227
[romantic string orchestra]

70
00:09:53,327 --> 00:09:54,762
But you are so young.

71
00:09:58,032 --> 00:10:01,702
And you know nothing
about Johnny Thunders.

72
00:10:04,839 --> 00:10:06,707
That father of mine.

73
00:10:08,609 --> 00:10:12,313
[romantic music continues]

74
00:10:26,260 --> 00:10:29,964
[Elle] He likes beautiful things
and beautiful people.

75
00:10:32,466 --> 00:10:34,268
He's a powerful man.

76
00:10:34,368 --> 00:10:36,605
[Johnny exhales]

77
00:10:36,704 --> 00:10:39,240
If you think he's playing games
with you...

78
00:10:41,576 --> 00:10:43,177
[chuckles]

79
00:10:43,277 --> 00:10:44,211
...he is.

80
00:10:46,147 --> 00:10:49,683
If you think he's being sincere
with you...

81
00:10:52,153 --> 00:10:53,087
...he is.

82
00:10:55,990 --> 00:10:58,659
Sometimes
he wants to impress you.

83
00:11:00,961 --> 00:11:03,764
Other times he wants
to be impressed by you.

84
00:11:05,366 --> 00:11:07,067
Usually the latter.

85
00:11:08,637 --> 00:11:11,305
In his mind,
you either have it or you don't.

86
00:11:14,308 --> 00:11:16,810
It must be genetic
because I'm the same way.

87
00:11:16,911 --> 00:11:19,947
[romantic music continues]

88
00:11:46,541 --> 00:11:49,176
[music fades]

89
00:11:57,418 --> 00:11:58,285
Ow!

90
00:11:59,588 --> 00:12:01,121
You pricked me.

91
00:12:01,690 --> 00:12:03,390
Oh, dear.

92
00:12:05,426 --> 00:12:06,827
I'm so sorry.

93
00:12:09,531 --> 00:12:10,397
Isn't it...

94
00:12:10,965 --> 00:12:13,200
a sign of good luck?

95
00:12:20,575 --> 00:12:23,978
[suspenseful music]

96
00:12:24,078 --> 00:12:26,413
As a matter of fact, it is.

97
00:12:34,021 --> 00:12:38,292
A prick of the needle is a sign
of... success.

98
00:12:49,937 --> 00:12:55,242
Fucking prick me, bitch.
Preferably...

99
00:12:55,342 --> 00:12:57,778
in the eye.

100
00:13:04,118 --> 00:13:08,956
Have you
experienced...misfortune?

101
00:13:11,825 --> 00:13:15,896
I am a victim of the mist.

102
00:13:28,442 --> 00:13:32,346
It is not the mist
you need to worry about,

103
00:13:33,748 --> 00:13:38,419
it is what the mist brings.

104
00:13:49,897 --> 00:13:54,134
[orchestral music continues]

105
00:14:07,716 --> 00:14:10,951
It's a tragedy if you ask me.

106
00:14:12,554 --> 00:14:15,989
Something no father
should have to endure.

107
00:14:16,090 --> 00:14:18,225
[tense, suspenseful music]

108
00:14:18,325 --> 00:14:19,594
I remember...

109
00:14:19,694 --> 00:14:21,362
the day that you were born.

110
00:14:25,734 --> 00:14:27,602
The day I saw the universe.

111
00:14:31,004 --> 00:14:33,006
My dear, Elle...

112
00:14:34,007 --> 00:14:35,909
I will always carry you.

113
00:14:36,711 --> 00:14:37,878
Always.

114
00:14:40,080 --> 00:14:42,650
I couldn't imagine losing you.

115
00:14:43,350 --> 00:14:46,654
But if I did, I'd search
the earth until my legs stopped
working.

116
00:14:50,057 --> 00:14:53,293
And if I had to
kill to find you,

117
00:14:53,394 --> 00:14:56,063
I'd do it.
And I'd keep on doing it.

118
00:14:56,163 --> 00:15:01,536
I would turn the oceans red
before I gave up on you.

119
00:15:06,106 --> 00:15:10,144
And that...my dear girls...

120
00:15:13,347 --> 00:15:17,251
...is the tragedy of The
Leatherman.

121
00:15:21,623 --> 00:15:22,657
Who?

122
00:15:29,062 --> 00:15:30,899
[sniffing]

123
00:15:30,998 --> 00:15:33,233
[exhaling heavily]

124
00:15:36,771 --> 00:15:42,943
The Leatherman is a father

125
00:15:43,043 --> 00:15:46,046
searching for his daughter
lost in the underworld.

126
00:15:46,146 --> 00:15:48,449
[ominous music]

127
00:15:48,550 --> 00:15:52,720
A father cursed to
search for lifetimes.

128
00:15:53,120 --> 00:15:55,422
Who eventually forgets
who he's looking for.

129
00:15:56,089 --> 00:15:57,224
[tense drone]

130
00:15:57,324 --> 00:16:02,262
But when the mist
returns, he remembers.

131
00:16:04,431 --> 00:16:05,733
He remembers her.

132
00:16:08,068 --> 00:16:10,805
He comes with the mist.

133
00:16:10,905 --> 00:16:12,306
Searching.

134
00:16:13,541 --> 00:16:14,876
His face...

135
00:16:14,975 --> 00:16:17,077
an infinite abyss.

136
00:16:17,879 --> 00:16:20,715
His strength insurmountable.

137
00:16:20,815 --> 00:16:24,886
He wears leather gloves
covered in razor sharp diamonds,

138
00:16:24,985 --> 00:16:26,119
searching for her

139
00:16:26,220 --> 00:16:27,722
and any girl who sees him.

140
00:16:27,822 --> 00:16:32,359
For when you see him, he sees
his daughter and he will try and

141
00:16:32,459 --> 00:16:35,697
destroy you and anyone
around you to get to her.

142
00:16:35,797 --> 00:16:37,765
And the only way to kill him...

143
00:16:40,400 --> 00:16:42,770
...is to cut off his hands.

144
00:16:42,871 --> 00:16:46,273
[tense orchestral music]

145
00:16:50,277 --> 00:16:53,280
That's why they say...

146
00:16:53,715 --> 00:16:58,987
take care of
your daughters. Or he will.

147
00:17:02,022 --> 00:17:05,092
[music fades]

148
00:17:05,192 --> 00:17:09,531
Daddy...is fascinating.

149
00:17:15,302 --> 00:17:16,771
[Elle] He's just a money guy.

150
00:17:17,972 --> 00:17:20,173
And you can call him Johnny.

151
00:17:24,746 --> 00:17:26,179
Okay.

152
00:17:28,783 --> 00:17:35,823
I wasn't expecting Johnny
to be like that one bit.

153
00:17:39,027 --> 00:17:42,797
[Hunter] He is so
curious and nurturing.

154
00:17:42,897 --> 00:17:44,599
He has this backwards logic

155
00:17:44,699 --> 00:17:48,503
where he thinks that fucking
girls my age will somehow bring
him closer to me.

156
00:17:51,405 --> 00:17:57,277
But didn't he,
like, marry Dominique?

157
00:17:58,345 --> 00:18:01,749
[soft romantic orchestral music]

158
00:18:32,379 --> 00:18:34,481
Why are you leaving me, Daddy?

159
00:18:34,582 --> 00:18:35,817
[music fades]

160
00:18:37,284 --> 00:18:40,120
[Johnny] I want you and
Dominique to be friends again.

161
00:18:43,423 --> 00:18:45,627
That's a sweet fantasy.

162
00:18:48,663 --> 00:18:50,865
Elle, making
a movie is like going to war.

163
00:18:52,934 --> 00:18:55,168
It'll bring you girls closer.

164
00:18:58,205 --> 00:19:01,475
I'm here because I wanted
to go to war with you.

165
00:19:03,377 --> 00:19:07,147
I would have never have agreed
to this if I knew you were
going to go.

166
00:19:08,482 --> 00:19:11,886
I'll only get in the way
of you two making up if I stay.

167
00:19:15,322 --> 00:19:18,860
You girls coming together
is how we become a family again.

168
00:19:21,294 --> 00:19:22,797
Dominique's one of us.

169
00:19:26,067 --> 00:19:29,704
She's like us,
but she's not one of us.

170
00:19:32,439 --> 00:19:33,841
There's a difference.

171
00:19:37,045 --> 00:19:39,279
She loves you something fierce.

172
00:19:41,248 --> 00:19:43,250
Maybe more
than she loves me.

173
00:19:51,358 --> 00:19:53,460
This movie's gonna be hell.

174
00:19:55,228 --> 00:19:56,931
[sighs]

175
00:19:59,834 --> 00:20:01,536
[Elle exhaling]

176
00:20:03,771 --> 00:20:06,774
[Elle sniffling]

177
00:20:10,144 --> 00:20:15,083
Promise me you'll be a good
girl and play nice while I'm
gone. Hmm?

178
00:20:15,183 --> 00:20:16,851
Hmm.

179
00:20:49,851 --> 00:20:53,487
[soft orchestral music]

180
00:21:46,107 --> 00:21:47,542
[music fades]

181
00:21:49,177 --> 00:21:51,879
[tense drone]

182
00:22:17,972 --> 00:22:21,876
[soft orchestral music]

183
00:23:07,387 --> 00:23:10,091
[Hunter laughs]

184
00:23:11,391 --> 00:23:14,494
[Hunter] What is she doing?

185
00:23:29,377 --> 00:23:33,114
[ominous drum]

186
00:23:43,391 --> 00:23:45,326
[screaming] Help me!

187
00:23:45,425 --> 00:23:47,395
Help me!

188
00:23:47,494 --> 00:23:49,797
Help me! Help--

189
00:23:49,897 --> 00:23:51,899
[woman's head
crashing into the window]

190
00:23:53,901 --> 00:23:55,002
[yelling] Daddy!

191
00:24:00,041 --> 00:24:02,009
[bones breaking]

192
00:24:18,458 --> 00:24:21,562
[tense orchestral music]

193
00:24:44,418 --> 00:24:48,089
[pulsating sound]

194
00:24:53,493 --> 00:24:54,895
[electronic button beep]

195
00:24:55,429 --> 00:24:57,898
[sweeping sound]

196
00:25:00,234 --> 00:25:02,737
[thrumming propulsion]

197
00:25:31,866 --> 00:25:34,869
[spaceship rattling heavily]

198
00:26:10,037 --> 00:26:12,706
[rattling fades]

199
00:26:16,377 --> 00:26:18,879
[ominous drone]

200
00:26:48,442 --> 00:26:51,645
[suspenseful music]

201
00:27:54,141 --> 00:27:56,143
[dramatic
orchestral music and laser fire]

202
00:28:14,128 --> 00:28:17,532
[dramatic
orchestral music fades]

203
00:28:17,632 --> 00:28:18,866
[thud]

204
00:28:18,966 --> 00:28:21,302
[calm orchestral music begins]

205
00:28:21,402 --> 00:28:22,637
[Elle groaning]

206
00:28:22,736 --> 00:28:26,840
[Elle breathing heavily]

207
00:28:41,855 --> 00:28:44,758
[Elle winces in pain]

208
00:28:51,198 --> 00:28:56,737
[dramatic
crescendo, then fading]

209
00:28:57,738 --> 00:28:59,507
Just kill me.

210
00:29:12,086 --> 00:29:13,120
I can't.

211
00:29:18,993 --> 00:29:21,161
I'm sorry, but...

212
00:29:23,897 --> 00:29:26,233
...do you guys
want to hear something scary?

213
00:29:26,333 --> 00:29:28,902
[tense high strings]

214
00:29:30,639 --> 00:29:34,041
[Hunter breathing heavily]

215
00:29:34,141 --> 00:29:38,145
[panting]

216
00:29:48,889 --> 00:29:53,260
I fell down the Leatherman
rabbit hole last night.

217
00:30:00,134 --> 00:30:06,874
And everything
Johnny said is true.

218
00:30:11,278 --> 00:30:12,346
And...

219
00:30:13,515 --> 00:30:16,150
there are these beings...

220
00:30:17,418 --> 00:30:20,789
called the kingmakers.

221
00:30:22,557 --> 00:30:26,994
This pair of women,
they always come in two.

222
00:30:28,697 --> 00:30:34,435
And they can be old or young.

223
00:30:35,936 --> 00:30:39,574
Hideous or beautiful.

224
00:30:41,308 --> 00:30:43,110
And sometimes...

225
00:30:43,578 --> 00:30:48,982
they can even
become shape shifting foxes.

226
00:30:50,150 --> 00:30:52,019
With multiple tails.

227
00:30:52,821 --> 00:30:54,355
Magic foxes?

228
00:30:54,455 --> 00:30:55,856
[Hunter] Yes.

229
00:30:56,256 --> 00:31:00,260
And they are the guides
for the Leatherman.

230
00:31:02,162 --> 00:31:05,567
And they are
neither good nor evil.

231
00:31:06,500 --> 00:31:07,635
Neutral.

232
00:31:09,637 --> 00:31:11,472
Morally ambiguous.

233
00:31:12,873 --> 00:31:15,075
[Hunter] This is legit.

234
00:31:15,610 --> 00:31:20,280
This leather guy
has been around for like, ever.

235
00:31:20,381 --> 00:31:24,251
Some cultures
call him the leather King,

236
00:31:25,119 --> 00:31:27,589
but most people...

237
00:31:30,491 --> 00:31:32,226
...call him...

238
00:31:33,427 --> 00:31:34,461
...the devil.

239
00:31:35,195 --> 00:31:39,266
Oh...no, not the devil.

240
00:31:40,835 --> 00:31:46,574
And it's these
magical lady foxes

241
00:31:46,674 --> 00:31:52,079
who help him find his destroyer.

242
00:31:53,815 --> 00:31:57,985
They are the ones who make him.

243
00:32:00,522 --> 00:32:03,957
And they are the ones...

244
00:32:04,057 --> 00:32:05,926
[high-pitched
voice] who end him!

245
00:32:12,199 --> 00:32:15,469
I just want you to understand

246
00:32:15,570 --> 00:32:20,340
that what we saw
was not a normal murder.

247
00:32:21,910 --> 00:32:23,944
[music fades]

248
00:32:24,044 --> 00:32:26,714
What the fuck
is a normal murder?

249
00:32:32,921 --> 00:32:36,524
I feel like you two should be
a bit more traumatized by this.

250
00:32:37,625 --> 00:32:40,494
Trauma comes in all forms.

251
00:32:43,197 --> 00:32:49,504
I mean, I couldn't even pretend
to kill Elle today.

252
00:32:52,540 --> 00:32:57,377
I really think
we saw the Leatherman.

253
00:32:59,914 --> 00:33:02,550
[suspenseful orchestral music]

254
00:33:32,145 --> 00:33:34,448
[music fades]

255
00:33:48,262 --> 00:33:50,030
[Johnny] <i>Elle.</i>

256
00:33:50,130 --> 00:33:52,800
[Johnny]  <i>Sad to miss</i>
<i>your big day tomorrow,</i>

257
00:33:52,901 --> 00:33:58,540
<i>but happy that we can bury</i>
<i>the hatchet.</i>
<i>Use it with love. Daddy.</i>

258
00:34:22,897 --> 00:34:23,898
[shower running]

259
00:34:23,998 --> 00:34:27,267
[orchestral music]

260
00:34:45,687 --> 00:34:46,621
[sigh]

261
00:35:02,070 --> 00:35:03,504
[music fades]

262
00:37:11,264 --> 00:37:14,135
[ominous, wind-like ambience]

263
00:37:14,234 --> 00:37:15,469
[lighter clicks shut]

264
00:37:21,209 --> 00:37:23,477
[exhales]

265
00:37:26,647 --> 00:37:29,282
[exhales]

266
00:37:58,579 --> 00:38:01,448
[suspenseful orchestral music]

267
00:38:50,397 --> 00:38:52,399
[Private K] <i>I</i>
<i>saw the Leatherman.</i>

268
00:38:54,202 --> 00:38:56,436
<i>I saw him take my daughter.</i>

269
00:39:00,141 --> 00:39:01,609
